		<!-- Image and Effects -->
		
		<Image imageID="&HS2_rsMakayevVoskhodII;" imageWidth="144" imageHeight="144"	rotationCount="360" rotationColumns="20" viewportRatio="0.2"/>
		<HeroImage imageID="&HS2_rsMakayevVoskhodIIHero;" imageWidth="320" imageHeight="320"/>

		<Effects>
			<Effect type="thrustMain"               posAngle="163"  posRadius="73"  posZ="0"        rotation="180"  effect="&efMainThrusterLarge;"/>
			<Effect type="thrustMain"               posAngle="-163" posRadius="73"  posZ="0"        rotation="180"  effect="&efMainThrusterLarge;"/>
			<Effect type="thrustMain"               posAngle="-180" posRadius="71"  posZ="24"       rotation="180"  effect="&efMainThrusterLarge;"/>
			<Effect type="thrustMain"               posAngle="-180" posRadius="71"  posZ="-24"      rotation="180"  effect="&efMainThrusterLarge;"/>
		</Effects>
		
		<!-- AI and Behavior -->

		<AISettings
			perception=			"4"
			combatStyle=		"standOff"
			/>
		
		<!-- Text -->
		
		<Language>
			<Text id="core.descLore">
				The Voskhod II is the pre-syrtis war ancestor to the Antares I. Designed
				alongside the Voskhod I, it used the same assembly facilities and parts,
				merely adding an additional cargo module to the front.

				While the modular construction kept the cost down, it also resulted in
				less-than-stellar structural integrity as the design grew longer, so
				Makayev engineers designed the common engine nacelles to help transfer
				loads from the forward cargo module by canting it at 45&deg; offset.
			</Text>
			<Text id="core.desc">
				The Voskhod II is an old, barebones heavy freighter. It has little in the
				way to offer in any regard, except for its massive cargo capacity.
			</Text>
		</Language>
	</ShipClass>
	
